A plain `.test { ... }` class you write yourself isn't a Tailwind utility, so variant prefixes like `md:` can't attach to it — that's why `md:test` does nothing. Register it with the `@utility` directive instead, and it will support variants automatically:

```css
@utility test {
  background: red;
}
```
```html
<h3 className="md:test">text</h3>
```

